# XSH va_start(), va_arg(), va_end() and va_copy()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The page only refers to XBD <stdarg.h>; the requirements tested come from
# that header's description (anchors below name this page, the requirements
# are in basedefs/stdarg.h.html). Each test uses its own variadic helper.

assertion  XSH.va_start.001
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       va_start() and va_arg() return the successive arguments in order,
           for int, long, long long, double, long double, pointer and
           struct-free argument lists, with char and short promoted to int
           and float promoted to double; a function called with no
           variable argument still can use va_start()/va_end().
test       t/001-in-order.c

assertion  XSH.va_start.002
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The mixes of type that are allowed work: an argument passed as a
           signed type is read as the corresponding unsigned type (value
           representable in both), and the other way round; a void pointer
           is read as a char pointer and the other way round.
test       t/002-compatible-types.c

assertion  XSH.va_start.003
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2008
says       On an XSI system arguments passed as one pointer type may be read
           as another pointer type (int * read as long *, then converted
           back).
note       The statement is XSI-shaded in the stdarg.h description.
test       t/003-pointer-types.c

assertion  XSH.va_start.004
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       va_copy() makes a copy that continues from the same point: after
           two arguments are read, the copy yields the remaining arguments in
           order, independently of further reads from the original, and
           both are ended with va_end().
test       t/004-copy.c

assertion  XSH.va_start.005
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A va_list may be passed to another function: vsnprintf() called
           with it formats the arguments, and after the call the caller
           passes the list only to va_end().
test       t/005-pass-to-function.c

assertion  XSH.va_start.006
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Several traversals, each bracketed by va_start() and va_end(),
           in one function give the same values each time.
test       t/006-multiple-traversals.c

assertion  XSH.va_start.007
anchor     functions/va_start.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A call with 24 variable arguments of mixed int, double and pointer
           types (more than fit in registers on any usual convention) reads
           back every value correctly.
test       t/007-many-args.c
